[
  {
    "slug": "stat-line-rerolling-strategy",
    "title": "Stat-line rerolling strategy",
    "category": "ideal-stat-lines",
    "summary": "Reroll materials, rare-line strategy, transfer cautions, and probability context.",
    "status": "source-uncertain",
    "sourceUrl": "https://docs.google.com/document/d/11u4wLCG1WfL-xSka2Aze0rI9vYRa7mq3N3Gp1bt0AWY/edit",
    "qualifiers": [
      "Source recommendations and first-person statements are Kanon’s. Captured update: 9/20/2026; Global changes were not all confirmed."
    ],
    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "block-0230",
        "sourceIds": ["block-0230"],
        "kind": "heading",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "CH 3: IDEAL STAT LINES"
          }
        ],
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "id": "block-0232",
        "sourceIds": ["block-0232"],
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Every piece of gear has “"
          },
          {
            "text": "Stat Lines",
            "strong": true
          },
          {
            "text": "” that comes on it. These "
          },
          {
            "text": "Stat Lines",
            "strong": true
          },
          {
            "text": " can be changed by using “Synch Stones” or other pieces of Gear of the equivalent grade (Yellow/Unique Synch Stones for Yellow/Unique gear). If you use lower grade Synch Stones (Yellow/Unique Synch Stone for an Orange/Heroic piece of gear, you will have a 10% chance for the stat to get rerolled"
          },
          {
            "text": " - never do this)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "block-0234",
        "sourceIds": ["block-0234"],
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Synch Stones are obtained via Substance Morphing either Synch Stone Fragments (mainly obtained by running dungeons) or any Yellow/Unique Gear piece."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "block-0236",
        "sourceIds": ["block-0236"],
        "kind": "figure",
        "figureId": "figure-019"
      },
      {
        "id": "block-0237",
        "sourceIds": ["block-0237"],
        "kind": "figure",
        "figureId": "figure-020"
      },
      {
        "id": "block-0240",
        "sourceIds": ["block-0240"],
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Another method of rerolling “"
          },
          {
            "text": "Stat Lines",
            "strong": true
          },
          {
            "text": "” is by using orange “Soul Codex: Reset” books (referred to as “Reset Books”). These reroll every single "
          },
          {
            "text": "Stat Line",
            "strong": true
          },
          {
            "text": " at once."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "block-0242",
        "sourceIds": ["block-0242"],
        "kind": "figure",
        "figureId": "figure-021"
      },
      {
        "id": "block-0244",
        "sourceIds": ["block-0244"],
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When rolling for lines on gear, always prioritize the lowest % roll lines (≈ x%"
          },
          {
            "text": " listed below)"
          },
          {
            "text": ".  It can be a nightmare fishing for the lower % lines especially on Heroic gear. If you get the BIS combination, you can  transfer your piece of gear into another using “Transfer Stones” to preserve your "
          },
          {
            "text": "Stat Lines",
            "strong": true
          },
          {
            "text": ". Try "
          },
          {
            "text": "to avoid getting a low % line on the extra Philosopher Stone line because that line will not carry over and you’ll have to fish for the line again."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "block-0246",
        "sourceIds": ["block-0246"],
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Be careful not to waste Orange/Heroic transfer Stones as these are much harder to come by. Transferring Yellow/Unique Gear to another Yellow/Unique Gear piece is pretty easy but put thought into transferring anything to Orange/Heroic gear. "
          },
          {
            "text": "(Check Chapter 5 - Transfer)",
            "emphasis": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "block-0248",
        "sourceIds": ["block-0248"],
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The following are the go-to "
          },
          {
            "text": "Stat Lines",
            "strong": true
          },
          {
            "text": " for every piece of gear in order of priority (priority from % chance to roll, not damage value. Ex: Weapon Damage Boost > Damage Boost in terms of actual damage value but Damage Boost will be listed higher on the list below because it has a lower % chance to roll). Percentages on each state vary from piece to piece but the relative difference is the same, you can use this as the benchmark to identify rarity amongst the "
          },
          {
            "text": "Stat Lines.",
            "strong": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "block-0250",
        "sourceIds": ["block-0250"],
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "(The following ",
            "emphasis": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Stat Lines",
            "strong": true,
            "emphasis": true
          },
          {
            "text": " are for Global)",
            "emphasis": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
